    "topic": "Merge Sort",
    "objective": "Show divide, sort halves and merge in order.",
    "learner": "Can read recursion and arrays.",
    "misconceptions": [
      "Merge sort reorders the array in place without using extra memory.",
      "Splitting an array sorts each piece immediately."
    ],
    "expectedUnderstanding": [
      "Splitting only divides the array; the pieces are not sorted by the split itself.",
      "Each half must be sorted before its elements can be merged into a sorted whole.",
      "The merge repeatedly takes the smaller front element, preserving order, and uses additional memory proportional to the array size."
    ]
  },
